
NETWORKS CHEAT SHEET - CORE (Ch. 1-25)
================================================================
FORMULAS
  d = L/C + dist/v + queue + proc        BDP = C x RTT
  U_s&w = 1/(1+2a), a = Tp/Tt            hosts = 2^(32-n) - 2
  Thru = min(C, W x MSS/RTT), need W >= BDP/MSS
  RTO = SRTT + 4 x RTTVAR                frag offset = bytes/8
  cwnd ~ sqrt(3/2p)     Thru ~ 1.22 x MSS/(RTT x sqrt(p))
  token delay <= beta/(C-r)              Little: L = lambda W
NUMBERS: min frame 64 B (payload 46) | max 1518/1500 | slot 512 bit-times
  IPv4 20 B | TCP 20 B | UDP 8 B | IPv6 40 B | MSS 1460 | TIME_WAIT 2 MSL
  alpha = 1/8, beta = 1/4 | cwnd0 = 1 MSS (modern 10)
PORTS 53 DNS | 67/68 DHCP | 69 TFTP | 161/162 SNMP | 179 BGP | 520 RIP
PROTO 1 ICMP | 6 TCP | 17 UDP | 89 OSPF
LAYERS: App (HTTP/DNS) > Transport (TCP/UDP) > Network (IP/ICMP/BGP)
  > Link (Ethernet/Wi-Fi) > Physical. ARP = L2/L3 boundary.
ETHERNET / LAN
  CSMA/CD: sense > send > collision > abort > backoff [0, 2^min(n,10)-1]
  slots. 64 B min so the sender still transmits at worst-case collision.
  Switch: learn src>port, forward known, flood unknown/broadcast, age out;
  splits collision, not broadcast, domains. VLAN 12-bit tag; trunk tagged.
  STP: root = lowest ID, block redundant links.
  Wi-Fi: CSMA/CA (no collision detect) + ACK after SIFS; RTS/CTS = hidden.
IP
  Header: Ver|IHL|DSCP|Len|ID|Flags|Off|TTL|Proto|Cksum|Src|Dst.
  TTL per hop; header checksum only; longest-prefix match.
  Private 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16 | loop 127/8 | link-local 169.254/16
  | multicast 224/4.
  Frag: offset in 8-byte units, MF=0 on last, reassemble at destination;
  DF > ICMP > PMTUD. NAT rewrites IP:port. ARP: IP>MAC in LAN. DHCP=DORA.
  ICMP = errors, no ports. DNS UDP/53.
  IPv6: 128-bit, 40-B header, no checksum, no router frag; NDP, SLAAC.
ROUTING
  DV: Bellman-Ford D_x(y) = min(c + D_v(y)); count-to-infinity >
  split horizon, poisoned reverse, triggered updates, path vector.
  LS: flood LSAs > topology > Dijkstra; fast, loop-free. ECMP hashes.
  CIDR: any prefix, longest match; aggregate contiguous blocks.
  BGP TCP/179: LOCAL_PREF > AS_PATH > ORIGIN > MED > eBGP>iBGP >
  IGP cost > router ID. AS_PATH loop detect; valley-free; anycast.
TCP
  Header 20 B: sport|dport|seq|ack|off|flags|win|cksum|urg|opts.
  Seq counts bytes. Flags URG ACK PSH RST SYN FIN. SYN > SYN-ACK > ACK.
  Random ISN. TIME_WAIT 2 MSL. Window = min(cwnd, rwnd).
  Nagle: 1 small unacked seg; delayed ACK ~200 ms; silly window:
  Clark + Nagle + persist. Karn: no RTT on retx; double RTO.
RENO
  cwnd < ssthresh    +1 MSS/ACK (doubles per RTT)
  cwnd >= ssthresh   +1 MSS/RTT
  timeout            ssthresh = cwnd/2, cwnd = 1
  3 dup (Tahoe)      ssthresh = cwnd/2, cwnd = 1
  3 dup (Reno)       ssthresh = cwnd/2, cwnd = ssthresh+3, inflate;
                     new ACK > cwnd = ssthresh
  Trace: 1>2>4>8>16>17 | timeout@24 > ssth 12, cwnd 1 > 2,4,8,12>13
  | 3 dup@20 > ssth 10, cwnd 13 > 10.
CONGESTION / QOS
  AIMD; Reno throughput ~ 1/RTT. RED: avg queue, min_th/max_th/max_p,
  early drop/mark. ECN marks instead of drops. Bufferbloat = big buffers.
  Token bucket (r, beta): burst <= beta; GCRA TAT = max(now,TAT)+L/r.
  WFQ finish-time order; Parekh-Gallager delay bound.
  IntServ per-flow RSVP; DiffServ DSCP/PHB; MPLS labels.
  Newer: Vegas delay | Westwood bw | Compound | Hybla | DCTCP ECN |
  CUBIC t^3 | BBR bw+RTT.
TRAPS
  propagation != transmission | min(cwnd, rwnd) | offset/8 | slow start
  exponential | timeout>1 vs 3 dup>halve | ssthresh = half current cwnd
  | TCP counts bytes | BGP policy first | count-to-infinity DV only |
  IPv6 no cksum/frag | RED != scheduler | token bucket bounds burst.
